{
  "program": "CBSTM03A",
  "caseId": "case04",
  "description": "5100-WRITE-HTML-HEADER (app/cbl/CBSTM03A.CBL:L506-L556) - the twenty-two HTMLFILE records that open every statement, pinned in their exact emission order. 5000-CREATE-STATEMENT reaches the paragraph through PERFORM 5100-WRITE-HTML-HEADER THRU 5100-EXIT at :L461, a benign range-PERFORM over a paragraph and its own matching exit label (:L554-L555 is nothing but EXIT), so it collapses to a single Java method call and carries no loop, no fall-through and no second entry point (rule R7). ORDER PINNED, 0-based HTMLFILE write indices: 0 HTML-L01, 1 HTML-L02, 2 HTML-L03, 3 HTML-L04, 4 HTML-L05, 5 HTML-L06, 6 HTML-L07, 7 HTML-L08, 8 HTML-LTRS, 9 HTML-L10, 10 HTML-L11, 11 HTML-LTDE, 12 HTML-LTRE, 13 HTML-LTRS, 14 HTML-L15, 15 HTML-L16, 16 HTML-L17, 17 HTML-L18, 18 HTML-LTDE, 19 HTML-LTRE, 20 HTML-LTRS, 21 HTML-L22-35. HTML-LTRS therefore appears three times (8, 13, 20) and HTML-LTDE twice (11, 18); the repeats are the point, because a paragraph that emitted one <tr> too few would still produce plausible HTML. Twenty-one of the twenty-two are WRITE FD-HTMLFILE-REC FROM HTML-FIXED-LN, and HTML-FIXED-LN is PIC X(100) (:L149), so each 88-level VALUE literal is right-padded with spaces to exactly 100 - the padding is encoded here explicitly, never implied (gate G21). THE ONE STRUCTURED RECORD: index 10 is written FROM HTML-L11 (:L530) after MOVE ACCT-ID TO L11-ACCT (:L529). HTML-L11 (:L212-L216) is a group of three spans - FILLER PIC X(34) VALUE '<h3>Statement for Account Number: ' + L11-ACCT PIC X(20) + FILLER PIC X(05) VALUE '</h3>' - so its declared width is 34 + 20 + 5 = 59, and because the FD record is PIC X(100) the WRITE right-pads it by 100 - 59 = 41 spaces. Both FILLER spans are emitted with their declared literals rather than treated as gaps; drop either and the record is short by exactly that span. L11-ACCT receives ACCT-ID PIC 9(11) (app/cpy/CVACT01Y.cpy) into a PIC X(20) field, and an integer moved to alphanumeric lands LEFT-JUSTIFIED and SPACE-PADDED, so the twenty bytes are '00000000001' followed by nine spaces - not right-aligned and not zero-extended. CONTINUATION LITERALS: HTML-L08 (:L157-L158), HTML-L10 (:L163-L164), HTML-L15 (:L165-L166) and HTML-L22-35 (:L173-L175) each span two source lines. Every continued fragment ends exactly at column 72, so the IBM rule that trailing blanks of a continued line belong to the literal contributes nothing, and the fragments join with NO character inserted: HTML-L08 keeps the double space in '<table  align=', and HTML-L10, HTML-L15 and HTML-L22-35 read 'padding:0px 5px;background-color:' with no space after the semicolon. SEEDS AND WHY THIS ROW: XREFFILE is seeded with 0-based row 48 of cardxref.txt, the one row of the fifty whose XREF-ACCT-ID is 00000000001 (card 9680294154603697, cust 000000001). 2000-CUSTFILE-GET keys on XREF-CUST-ID (:L372-L374) and 3000-ACCTFILE-GET on XREF-ACCT-ID (:L396-L398), so this row alone drives the statement off the FIRST record of acctdata.txt and the FIRST of custdata.txt, and it is what puts 00000000001 in L11-ACCT. cardxref.txt rows stay 36 bytes: CVACT03Y declares 50 and the fixture omits the trailing FILLER PIC X(14), and the 36-to-50 pad is declared once under normalisations because the seeding side owns it (gate G16). TRNXFILE is INLINE - app/data/ASCII holds exactly nine .txt fixtures and none of them is a TRNXFILE - so three 350-byte COSTM01 records are supplied here (32-byte TRNX-KEY + 318-byte TRNX-REST closing on a space-filled FILLER PIC X(20)), ascending by card then id as STEP010's SORT FIELDS=(263,16,CH,A,1,16,CH,A) leaves them. SIBLING PARAGRAPHS ARE NOT THIS CASE'S SUBJECT: 5200-WRITE-HTML-NMADBS (:L486, 34 records), 6000-WRITE-TRANS (11 records per transaction) and the footer in 4000-TRNXFILE-GET (:L439-L454, 8 records) belong to case05, case01/case20 and case06. They are still pinned here, because a row the unit writes and no expectation addresses is itself a parity failure, and because a case has to describe a whole run to describe one paragraph honestly. The counts are arithmetic, not guesswork: HTMLFILE = 22 + 34 + 11N + 8 = 64 + 11N and STMTFILE = 1 + 15 + N + 3 = 19 + N, which at N=3 transactions is 97 and 22. WIDTHS: HTMLFILE is 100 bytes - 01 FD-HTMLFILE-REC PIC X(100) at :L47 and DCB=(LRECL=100,BLKSIZE=800,RECFM=FB) at app/jcl/CREASTMT.JCL:L94, under the HTMLFILE DD of the creating step at :L92. That supersedes STEP030's IEFBR14 pre-delete LRECL=80,BLKSIZE=3200 at :L69 - the creating step wins (risk R-G). STMTFILE is 80 bytes, from 01 FD-STMTFILE-REC PIC X(80) at :L45 and DCB=(LRECL=80,BLKSIZE=8000,RECFM=FB) at CREASTMT.JCL:L89. Line 90 of that JCL is genuinely corrupted - it reads 'SPACE=(CYL,(1,1),RLSE), 00,RECFM=FB), ATA.VSAM.KSDS' - and its ' 00,RECFM=FB)' remnant sits directly beneath STMTFILE where it is easily misread as LRECL=100, which would widen the text statement to 100 and break every one of its twenty-two rows. It is not data, it is not corrected, and the widths are cited from lines 89 and 94 instead. UNIT AND INVOCATION: statement.StatementGenerationJobA as a BATCH_JOB at step/Tasklet level with statement.StatementGenerationJobB as its constructor-injected collaborator - no JobLauncher, no job repository, no HTTP (gate G51). jobParameters is empty because CREASTMT.JCL declares no PARM on any of its five steps, and STEP040 (:L79), the step that runs CBSTM03A, is no exception. expectedReturnCode is 0: no DISPLAY-and-abend arm of 1000-XREFFILE-GET-NEXT, 2000-CUSTFILE-GET, 3000-ACCTFILE-GET or 8500-READTRNX-READ is reached, so 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM (:L916-L923) never runs. PROVENANCE: every expected value here is STATICALLY DERIVED - the 88-level literals and the HTML-L11 spans read from the bytes of app/cbl/CBSTM03A.CBL, the record widths from app/cpy/COSTM01.CPY, CVACT01Y.cpy, CUSTREC.cpy and CVACT03Y.cpy, the output widths from app/jcl/CREASTMT.JCL, and the account, customer and cross-reference values from the real app/data/ASCII fixtures. Nothing was captured from an execution of the legacy COBOL, which is impossible in this environment.",
